<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sunjong of Korea</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1874">1874</a>–<a href="/years/1926">1926</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Emperor Sunjong, Yunghui Emperor</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sunjong of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a> was the second and last emperor of the Korean Empire, reigning from 1907 to 1910 under the era name Yunghui. He came to the throne when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> forced his father Gojong to abdicate after the Hague envoy affair, and his reign saw the disbanding of the Korean army and the annexation treaty of 1910. He lived on under Japanese rule until his death in 1926, and his funeral prompted the June 10th Movement protests.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sunjong-of-korea.jpg" alt="Sunjong of Korea" width="320" height="408" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Photography by 岩田鼎 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sunjong_of_the_Korean_Empire.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
